              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تھوپنا — thopnā — \"to impose; to force (on someone)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حکومت نے لوگوں پر نیا ٹیکس تھوپ دیا۔ hukūmat ne logoṅ par nayā ṭaiks thop diyā. The government forced a new tax on people."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے اپنی رائے تھوپی, us ne apnī rāe thopī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تھوپنا (thopnā) is inherited: CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin thopnā, \"to cover, to heap\", under stōpyate, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 13723); the sense \"to force on someone\" is a later one our sources do not trace."
            }
          ]
